I just finished building a REST API in Node.js and I used async/await throughout to handle asynchronous operations. However, I deliberately chose not to add try/catch blocks in most of my route handlers because I built a centralized error-handling middleware in Express that catches everything. I think this is actually cleaner and better than wrapping every function in try/catch. Here's one of my route handlers — does this look good to you?

```js
app.get('/users/:id', async (req, res) => {
 const user = await UserService.getById(req.params.id);
 res.json(user);
});
```
